{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>ע</b> of Shema is large: Israel has 70 names, and He gave them Torah which has 70 names and is expounded in 70 facets, to distinguish from the 70 nations. And there is a break between YHWH and אחד to say: even though you saw many apparitions, and even though I come with this in strict justice — with this in abundant mercy — nevertheless all is one. <b>אחד</b> — the dalet is large, to tell you that you should enthrone Him in heaven and earth and in the four directions of the world, and also that you not err in the resh. And so the resh of לא תשתחוה לאל אחר is large, so you not err in the dalet. Another interpretation: ע and dalet are large — הרי עד (witness), and this is <b>ואתם עדי נאם ה'</b>, and also the Holy One, blessed be He, is a witness to Israel, as written <b>והייתי עד ממהר</b>. <b>שמע</b> — in gematria ת\"י שת\"י (411), [meaning] two years [Jacob] spent [in the academy of Shem and Eber]. The verse begins with shin and ends with dalet — הרי שד (demons), [so that] the demons flee from the one who recites Shema with proper intention."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:00.531595060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}